Z||000000||Dingo||03-27-2001||07:26 PM||||Ok now I am ready for some of the usual questions. <P>1) Who sales the best suspension kit for a 1988 Fiero GT. Will it lower the car?<BR>2) What size rims can I fit under my car when it comes to 17" and 18" rims. What width and any offsets.<BR>3) What size rubber can I fit on those rims and are they going to rub?<BR>4) Who sales the Indy Scoop and URL with prices. I found one but the page was not working so I could not find the price.<BR>5) Northstar or Turbo 3800? They both sound like great options.<BR>6) Best way to go with the disc brakes.<P>How will the motor conversion affect the suspion kits and other upgrades mentioned above. I want the car to handle at its best and kick the crap out of the japanese cars. I am sick of honda, nissan, etc. hmmm... How about a turbo northstar?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)<P>Im more interested in 1/4mi times and 0-100 as well as handling like a race car. hmmm is 1G lateral expecting to much? I remember a few years back a company out of Oregon called Pegasus Engineering. I think they sold a suspension kit that they claimed would give the Fiero 1G or better.<P>thanks||||reg||10
Z||000001||Nashco||03-27-2001||08:03 PM||||You seem to have made a lot of posts lately about things we're always talking about here and there.  Since your new, I thought I'd let you know there's a search function for the website.  On this page you're looking at right now, in the upper right corner there's a link that says "search" that you need to go to.  Just enter the forum you want to look in, and the keyword for the search (such as suspension, or 18", or indy scoop).  This will save you a lot of time, because a lot of this stuff has been gone through before in the past.  It will also clear up some space on the forum so we're not doubling up on topics.  I hope this works out for ya, I know it helped me a lot <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||03-27-2001||09:52 PM||||all that stuff you want to do will cost you like $20K,   I would go with eather a Northstar or a Supercharged Series II 3800 (/w aftermarket supercharger pullly)<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-28-2001||11:06 AM||||Indy scoop. <BR>IRM<BR>cost $200<BR>1-800-367-8423<BR>or<BR>1-301-948-3301<BR>or <BR>Email: IRMFIERO@aol.com<BR>They don't have a website but the link below goes to a copy of their catalog.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html</A> <P>The next link sells the scoop but they call it an SD4 street scoop. Cost is $189.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P>FOCOA sells them but they want over $300 for them. I don't have a link to the parts page.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||03-28-2001||11:38 AM||||All I can tell is you search for the tire stuff, there's like a 50 reply tire thread every other day here.<P>About the lowering part, I would do coil overs, <A HREF="http://www.ground-control.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ground-control.com</A>  and <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.heldmotorsports.com</A>  for the fronts.  Just add poly every where else too <A HREF="http://www.suspensionl.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspensionl.com</A>  and your set. <P>Not sure what you mean about the brakes, but when I give in and get rims, I am just going to get the cross drilled rotors from the Fiero Store and paint my calipers.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||montage||03-28-2001||02:58 PM||||I am also interested in information on the width and offset of wheels that can be used on 88's. I did several searches of the forum and could not find any info particularly on the offset people use. I did determine that an 8" wheel with a 245 tire is the widest one can go on a stock car on the rear but no info on offset used was given. In addition, I couldn't find any comments on offset used on the front of the 88 and how it looks.||||reg||1
